 "notes": "Final1. One seg.evaluate_ensemble process (slurm step on sdfada013 idx1, 46.6 min): each of 4 candidate checkpoints (r34 best/last, UNet++ best/last) predicted once per val image with 4-flip TTA; 9 member subsets x 21 thresholds scored with seg.evaluate.Accumulator on 300 evenly spaced val images; best = {r34 last, UNet++ best} at thr 0.70 (val peak F1 0.9251; best single on val: UNet++ best 0.9248). Then the WHOLE test split (1529 images) with that subset + threshold only. Test peak F1 0.9182 (P .898, R .940). Independent check: h8 re-scored the saved test prob maps ($PK/runs/h7/final/test_probs_final1, float16) with separate code and got the same TP/FP/FN. History: 0.9061 (r34 step-6000 snapshot, no TTA) -> 0.9141 (UNet++ best alone, no TTA) -> 0.9182 (this). Findings: full-res decoders matter for 1-2 px peaks; FPs are confident 1-2 px spots far from labeled peaks that look like real unlabeled peaks, so precision is capped near 0.9 by the labels; min-size/closing post-processing did not help; flip TTA +0.002; saturated-pixel masking no effect for these models; val F1 fluctuates +-0.03 between checkpoints, so checkpoint choice on val matters.",
